Atlas overlay patch 0013: brand/policy-directory
Why: the engine reads system-wide policy files from /etc/chromium/policies; the platform branding
patch renames the data directory, desktop file and environment variables but not this one. WolOS
ships its policies (crates/core/src/browser.rs) in /etc/atlas/policies/{managed,recommended}, so
without this line the browser reads none of them. One string, no logic.
Files: components/policy/core/common/policy_paths.cc
Test filter: atlas/tests/test_series.sh; on a dev slot, a managed policy file in /etc/atlas/policies/managed is read (chrome://policy lists it)
Rebase risk: L (one string in a stable file)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunk in a file the inherited series touches or may touch)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

--- a/components/policy/core/common/policy_paths.cc
+++ b/components/policy/core/common/policy_paths.cc
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ const char kPolicyPath[] = "/etc/opt/chrome/policies";
 #elif BUILDFLAG(GOOGLE_CHROME_FOR_TESTING_BRANDING)
 const char kPolicyPath[] = "/etc/opt/chrome_for_testing/policies";
 #else
-const char kPolicyPath[] = "/etc/chromium/policies";
+const char kPolicyPath[] = "/etc/atlas/policies";
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING)
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_POSIX) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
 
